# The sources of the libmpv that Patina.app is to carry, each pinned by
# digest, and of the two tools the build needs that macOS doesn't have.
# Read by packaging/macos-libmpv-build.sh, which builds them into one
# universal (arm64 and x86_64) set of dylibs for macOS 11, with sed rather
# than by sourcing this file, so nothing here is ever run. FFmpeg's pin is
# not here: it stays in bundled-tools.env, shared with packaging/ffmpeg.sh,
# so that one bump moves both the ffmpeg in Contents/Helpers and the
# libav* libraries libmpv links.
#
# For now only .github/workflows/macos-libmpv.yml builds from these, to show
# that the build works; release.yml still ships IINA's libraries
# (packaging/macos-libmpv.txt) until it is switched over.
#
# Every name has three lines: NAME_VERSION, NAME_URL and NAME_SHA256. A
# GitHub archive (refs/tags or a commit) is pinned for a project that
# publishes no tarball of its own; GitHub has kept those bytes stable for
# years, and the digest is what fails if it ever doesn't. The script prints
# the digest it computed when one doesn't match, so to bump a pin, change
# the version and the URL, run `packaging/macos-libmpv-build.sh fetch <dir>`
# (on any machine; it downloads every source and checks each digest, and
# runs nothing it downloads), and check the new file before writing its
# digest:
#
#   Signed upstream: check the signature in a keyring of its own,
#       export GNUPGHOME=$(mktemp -d)
#       gpg --keyserver hkps://keyserver.ubuntu.com --recv-keys <the key>
#       gpg --verify <the .asc or .sig> <the tarball>
#     and check that the key is the one named below, or, if it has changed,
#     that the project says so on its own site.
#     - mpv: the .asc attached to the GitHub release
#       (https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/releases/download/v<version>/mpv-<version>.tar.gz.asc)
#       signs the refs/tags archive below. mpv names no single release key:
#       0.42.0's is Kacper Michajłow's, DE537FA4CD83E657227D6461D6CA75F6505F42A5
#       (signing subkey D83F25E44BD6B948724AB75F6580132338ABD4E2), as
#       windows-deps.env says for the Windows libmpv, and the key has to
#       belong to an mpv maintainer in the same way.
#     - libass: <URL>.asc, 0.17.5's by Oneric,
#       5EE63F2A71BF132CFE3567E1DFFE615F2824C720.
#     - freetype: <URL>.sig, by Werner Lemberg,
#       E30674707856409FF1948010BE6C3AAC63AD8E3F.
#     - dav1d: <URL>.asc, by the VideoLAN Release Signing Key (2018),
#       65F7C6B4206BD057A7EB73787180713BE58D1ADC. The key has expired since
#       it signed 1.5.4, so gpg calls it expired and the signature good.
#     - OpenSSL: <URL>.asc, by OpenSSL's own key,
#       B146647E45A7B33947AB226B2A2C87D161692D40.
#     - libwebp: <URL>.asc, by the WebP release signing key,
#       6B0E6B70976DE303EDF2F601F9C3D6BDB8232B5D.
#   Not signed: harfbuzz and fribidi (GitHub release assets, whose digest
#     the release lists: gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/releases/tags/<tag>
#     --jq '.assets[] | "\(.name) \(.digest)"'), uchardet, nasm and pkgconf
#     (their projects' own download sites, which publish no signatures),
#     and the GitHub archives. For those, the file has to come from the
#     project's own repository or site as the URL shows, and a commit has to
#     be one the project's history holds.
#
# libplacebo's four submodules come with it: a GitHub archive of a tag has
# no submodules in it, so each is pinned at the commit libplacebo's tag
# names, which, after bumping libplacebo, this prints:
#   gh api 'repos/haasn/libplacebo/contents/3rdparty?ref=v<version>' --jq '.[] | "\(.name) \(.sha)"'
# glad, jinja and markupsafe generate libplacebo's OpenGL loader and shaders
# at build time; fast_float is a header it compiles in. Vulkan-Headers and
# json.h aren't needed: the build has no Vulkan, and json.h is in the
# tarball itself.
#
# LuaJIT has no releases, only a rolling v2.1 branch, so it is pinned at a
# commit of that branch. Its archive carries .relver, from which LuaJIT
# takes its version, so jit.version names the commit's time.
#
# What each must be at least, from mpv 0.42.0's meson.build: FFmpeg 6.1
# (libavcodec 60.31.102), libplacebo 7.387.0, libass 0.12.2 and, for the
# Lua scripts Patina needs, LuaJIT 2.0. A newer mpv usually raises the
# libplacebo floor too.

MPV_VERSION=0.42.0
MPV_URL=https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/archive/refs/tags/v0.42.0.tar.gz
MPV_SHA256=bcfebbfa2b65a6d88dc97ea18117831072373e38b5785a2afb874ed4df5070dd

LIBPLACEBO_VERSION=7.387.0
